# WFORMTA.KEY - typing into every type of field: the form of every type
# of TEST/WFORMT.C in edit mode, then in view mode, then in new mode,
# where its FF_NEWONLY field can be changed, then the fields reached by
# their access letters in edit and view mode;
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WFORMTA.SNP.
K F5
S OPEN
# Text, a code folded to upper case, two numbers, a date with its
# hyphens, the check box, a row of each drop-down list.
T Mixed Case
K TAB
T b2x
K TAB
T 12
K TAB
T 1234.50
K TAB
T 1983-11-01
K TAB SPACE TAB DOWN TAB DOWN
S CHOSEN
# ID (FF_RO) and Serial (FF_NEWONLY) take the focus but no typing.
K TAB
T zz
K TAB
T qq
S READONLY
# The password, edited, and a third line of the memo, on the Notes page,
# by CTRL-ENTER.
K TAB
T Secret1x
K BS
K CTRL-TAB CEND CTRL-ENTER
T Third line
S TYPED
K ENTER
S SAVED
# View mode shows what was typed, the focus on the strip, which takes
# no letter but its tabs'; nothing can be changed, in the memo neither,
# which TAB reaches on the Notes page.
K F6
S VIEW
T abc
K CTRL-TAB TAB CEND
T abc
K CTRL-ENTER BS DEL
S VIEWRO
K ENTER
# New mode: Serial can be changed, and the memo starts empty.
K F7
K TAB TAB TAB TAB TAB TAB TAB TAB TAB
T sn-9
S NEW
K ENTER
K F6
S VIEW2
K ESC
S DONE
# Access letters in edit mode: Alt and a label's letter moves the focus
# to its field, whatever its type, and from the check box, which takes
# no characters, the letter alone does; the ID, which cannot be
# changed, has no letter, so ALT-I leaves the focus where it is.
K F5
K ALT-O
S ALTO
K P
S ALONE
K ALT-C
S ALTC
K ALT-I
S ALTI
K ALT-N
S ALTN
K ENTER
# In view mode no label shows a letter, so Alt and a field's edit-mode
# letter moves nothing, the focus staying on the strip.
K F6
K ALT-I
S VIEWALTI
K ALT-S
S VIEWALTS
K ESC
